# Folkprotocol Protocol Dossiers v0
#
# Fourth experimental slice. It performs bounded, targeted research for only
# the selected protocol directions and reconstructs exact practices. It does
# not draft the public page.

Expect slug
Default work_dir: /home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol

Work in {work_dir}

Codex: """Build protocol dossiers for the selected directions in
research/source-maps/{slug}/80-practice-assessment.md.

Required local inputs are 00-commission.md, the six source maps from 10 through
60, 70-practice-strains.md, and 80-practice-assessment.md. Verify all completion
markers first. If any required file is absent or incomplete, do not write the
output; report the exact path and stop.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 00-commission.md 10-reddit-forums.md 20-traditional.md
30-published-research.md 40-commercial-web.md 50-experimental-communities.md
60-practitioner-folk-web.md 70-practice-strains.md
80-practice-assessment.md | sha256sum`. Write
research/source-maps/{slug}/90-protocol-dossiers.md with that digest in YAML
frontmatter as inputDigest. If a complete output already records the same
digest and is at most 6,000 words, leave it unchanged. Rebuild when the digest
changes.

Work on this pass yourself. Do not delegate, spawn subagents, or launch Mill,
Spindle, Horizon, or another agent workflow. Write only the output file. Web
research is allowed, but only to answer the targeted questions in the
assessment. Prefer direct sources: the actual paper, thread, product label,
traditional text or close scholarly translation, regulatory record, or named
practitioner account. Search results and reviews may locate a source but should
not replace an accessible original. Mark an inaccessible source honestly.

Reconstruct only the 4–7 selected directions. Do not add a dossier merely
because a new remedy appears during research. Put genuinely relevant adjacent
findings in a short `Research spillover` section instead.

For each direction establish, where the record permits:

- the exact practice, preparation, or product specification; distinguish plant
  part, extract, formulation, route, and branded preparation when they matter
- timing and amount actually used in a study, tradition, label, or recurring
  community practice; do not manufacture a dose from mechanism alone
- which outcome or symptom people claim or observed, the size and timing of the
  effect when stated, and what kind of source produced that statement
- the likely operative pathway, clearly separating the source's own explanation
  from a later mechanistic interpretation; a practice can remain interesting
  when its folk explanation is wrong
- disagreements, null reports, preparation mismatches, and circumstances that
  plausibly explain divergent outcomes
- concrete boundaries that materially change use. Do not pad every dossier
  with generic warnings or turn it into withdrawal care
- an `ordinary-use test` describing what a noticeable result would look like
  over normal use. Do not prescribe spreadsheets, symptom scales, fixed alcohol
  challenges, or a quantified-self regimen

Treat heterogeneous evidence in context. Do not require cross-domain
convergence. Do not apologize for traditional or forum material by repeatedly
holding it against clinical literature. Conversely, do not upgrade repetition,
longevity, biochemical vocabulary, patents, or sales copy into validation.

Use two citation systems without mixing them:

- Retain cross-map citations such as [10:RF12] when describing what the map
  found.
- Assign direct-source citations [P1], [P2], and so on for sources opened in
  this pass. Every exact amount, timing, outcome, mechanistic claim, preparation
  distinction, or risk statement must cite a direct source. One ID names one
  retrievable item.

End with `Direct source index`, recording for every [Pn]: title, author or
owner, date, stable URL/DOI/PMID, access status, source kind, which dossier it
supports, and a short description of what was actually taken from it. Do not
quote more than 25 words from any non-forum source or more than 10 words of song
lyrics. Forum quotations may be longer when useful but should remain brief.

End the file with `DOSSIERS COMPLETE — N directions, M direct sources`, using
actual counts. Run wc -w and shorten until the file is at most 6,000 words
without dropping protocol-critical details or citations.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, permission=research, research_target=file:/home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol/research/source-maps/{slug}/90-protocol-dossiers.md, timeout=2400
